DATA SOURCE NOTE (no silent drift)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt's data-source block reads "(no API data sources — renders from
navigation values / local state)". The web source DOES load data —
`useQuery(['vampire-drain-stats', id]) -> GET /vampire-drain/stats?vehicle_id` via
`useSelectedVehicle()` — and the manifest record declares the loading/error/success
states accordingly. The generator's classifier simply missed the inline `request()`
(it is not a named `use*` hook file). The page is therefore bound through an
`@Observable VampireDrainPageModel` + a `VampireDrainDataSource` seam (ADR-004), with
the full loading / empty / error / success phase machine, exactly like the sibling
SleepEfficiency surface. No networking lives in the view.

