This repo pins Swift 6.0; the available runner is the NEWER Xcode 26.5 (Swift 6.x), whose
stricter actor-isolation front-end rejects several PRE-EXISTING, out-of-scope test files
that are UNMODIFIED by this change (verified via `git status`) and outside this artifact's
allowed files. The repo documents macOS verification as PENDING
(apps/macos-pending-verifications.md). Examples encountered on a clean tree (all unmodified
by this change, all in the `TeslaSync-macOSTests` bundle):
  - Tests/Unit/Features/Analytics/TimelinePageModelTests.swift:318
      "call to main actor-isolated static method 'utcDayKey' in a synchronous nonisolated context"
  - Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/VehicleCostPageModelTests.swift:10
      "main actor-isolated default value in a nonisolated context"
  - Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift:20  (the predecessor's finding)
      "call to main actor-isolated static method ... in a synchronous nonisolated context"
These are an environment/toolchain mismatch, not a code defect, and pre-date this change.

To exercise THIS page's tests without editing any out-of-scope file, the test target was
narrowed to ONLY this change's two relevant test classes via the command-line build settings
  EXCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES='*Tests.swift'
  INCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES='VampireDrainPageModelTests.swift RouteTests.swift'
(a build override, no source edits — every other *Tests.swift is dropped from compilation,
the two needed are re-included). With that, the app target builds clean and this page's 17
tests + the 8 routing tests all pass (above). No VampireDrain / AppRoute / AppRouteParser /
TeslaSyncApp file produced any diagnostic.

IMPORTANT: the app `build` action itself needs NO exclusions — `xcodebuild ... build`
